  "pregnancyDisclaimer": "Dates are estimated from your last period using the standard 280-day rule. An ultrasound gives a more accurate date, and late ovulation shifts these numbers — this is information, not medical care.",
  "pregnancyNoteUnder5": "Most people notice nothing yet — because gestational age counts from your last period, the first two weeks are actually before conception.",
